    "body": "Thanks for the review!  \r\n\r\nDo you mean changing the code like this?  \r\n\r\n```zsh\r\nif [[ -n $__starship_preserved_zle_keymap_select ]]; then\r\n    zle -N zle-keymap-select $__starship_preserved_zle_keymap_select;\r\nfi\r\n__starship_preserved_zle_keymap_select=${widgets[zle-keymap-select]#user:}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI actually considered this too. However, I think it may cause an issue.  \r\n\r\nFor example, consider this `.zshrc`:  \r\n\r\n```zsh\r\nbindkey -v\r\nfunction myfoo() {\r\n        echo \"\\nfoo\\n\"\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction mybar() {\r\n        echo \"\\nbar\\n\"\r\n}\r\nzle -N zle-keymap-select myfoo\r\neval \"$(~/github-project/starship/target/debug/starship init zsh)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf the user later wants to change `zle-keymap-select` to `mybar`, then `source .zshrc`:\r\n\r\n```zsh\r\n--- zle -N zle-keymap-select myfoo\r\n+++ zle -N zle-keymap-select mybar\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis would cause the user’s changes to disappear.  \r\n\r\nMaybe I misunderstood your suggestion; please pointer it out if that’s the case.",
